  "@type": "urpx:URPXPackage",
  "@id": "sdge:doc-ev-tou-2-2026-04-01",
  "urpx:targetURPXVersion": "https://github.com/urpx-org/urpx/raw/v0.5.1/ontology/urpx-ontology.ttl",
  "urpx:hasRatePlan": {
    "@type": "urpx:RatePlan",
    "@id": "sdge:ev-tou-2",
    "urpx:name": "Schedule EV-TOU-2 Domestic Time-of-Use for Households with Electric Vehicles",
    "urpx:ratePlanUniqueIdentifier": "EV-TOU-2",
    "urpx:initialEffectiveDate": "2016-01-01",
    "urpx:timezoneIdentifier": "America/Los_Angeles",
    "urpx:hasRatePlanVersion": {
      "@type": "urpx:RatePlanVersion",
      "@id": "sdge:ev-tou-2-2026-04-01",
      "urpx:description": "SDG&E's middle-vintage EV-charging-targeted residential TOU schedule (predecessor to EV-TOU-5; successor to EV-TOU). Per Sheet 1 applicability prose, EV-TOU-2 is 'specifically limited to customers who require service for charging of a currently registered Motor Vehicle... 1) a battery electric vehicle (BEV) or plug-in hybrid electric vehicle (PHEV) recharged via a recharging outlet at the customer's premises; or 2) a natural gas vehicle (NGV) refueled via a home refueling appliance (HRA) at the customer's premises.' Unlike EV-TOU, EV-TOU-2 does NOT require separate metering of EV charging — customer's whole-premise consumption is billed on this rate. Same TOU window structure as TOU-DR1/EV-TOU/EV-TOU-5 (on-peak 4-9pm every day; super-off-peak weekday split midnight-6am + 10am-2pm, weekend continuous midnight-2pm). Has the modern Base Services Charge structure (standard $0.79343/day, DRAH/FERA $0.39688, CARE $0.19713) — same as TOU-DR1 and EV-TOU-5. UDC Total has TOU signal: $0.31343/kWh on-peak/off-peak (Distribution component $0.19763); $0.17246/kWh super-off-peak (Distribution $0.05666). UDC sub-components: Transmission $0.10067 (flat — like EV-TOU; unlike EV-TOU-5 which has Transmission TOU-varying), Distribution $0.19763/$0.05666 (TOU-varying), PPP $0.01515, ND $0.00000, CTC -$0.00007, LGC $0.00000, RS $0.00005, TRAC $0.00000. EECC values match EV-TOU and EV-TOU-5 exactly: Summer On-Peak $0.47019, Off-Peak $0.17311, Super-Off-Peak $0.08147; Winter On-Peak $0.19990, Off-Peak $0.14337, Super-Off-Peak $0.07410. NO Baseline Adjustment Credit (consistent with EV-TOU and EV-TOU-5). Climate Credit $(49.36) per Schedule GHG-ARR semi-annually (mentioned in Sheet 1 prose; not modeled here as a per-period Price). 12-month minimum stay rule (Special Condition 5). PCIA recovery in bundled EECC rates (Special Condition 10). CCA-served customers pay UDC + DWR-BC + WF-NBC + their CCA's generation rate. Franchise Fee Differential of 5.78% applies to City of San Diego customers.",
      "urpx:effectiveDateTime": "2026-04-01T00:00:00",
      "urpx:minimumTenure": "P12M",
      "urpx:changeReason": {
        "@id": "urpx:rateCase"
      },
      "urpx:priceCurrency": "USD",
      "urpx:commodity": {
        "@id": "urpx:electricity"
      },
      "urpx:serviceRole": {
        "@id": "urpx:bundledServiceRole"
      },
      "urpx:customerChoice": {
        "@id": "urpx:voluntaryChoice"
      },
      "urpx:isDefault": false,
      "urpx:hasDataSourceReference": {
        "@type": "urpx:DataSourceReference",
        "urpx:fileName": "SDGE_SCHEDULE_EV-TOU-2.pdf",
