      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "sdge:cc-ev-tou-2-2026-04-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "sdge:cc-ev-tou-2-2026-04-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "Four provisions of the published Schedule EV-TOU-2 are not represented in this filing. The Franchise Fee Differential of 5.78 percent applied to monthly billings for all customers within the corporate limits of the City of San Diego. The semi-annual California Climate Credit of $49.36 under Schedule GHG-ARR, named in the applicability section. The Direct Access and Community Choice Aggregation bill path of Special Condition 8.b, under which the bill is computed as though bundled and then credited by the EECC and DWR-BC components, with the applicable Cost Responsibility Surcharge added; what is modeled is the bundled path, and its EECC rate per Special Condition 10 already embeds the Power Charge Indifference Adjustment. And the Special Condition 5 bar on returning to the schedule for one year after leaving, where the twelve-month minimum stay from the same condition is recorded. The Base Services Charge variants published on Sheets 1 and 2 for CARE ($0.19713 per day), FERA and DRAH ($0.39688 per day each) are carried by separate overlay filings rather than missing; the standard $0.79343 per day charge is modeled here. The remaining special conditions are out of scope rather than missing: standard lighting voltage (1), welder ratings (2), meter ownership and location (3), the fallback to the otherwise applicable domestic schedule when the meter's timing device fails (4), Optional Billing at the utility's sole option (7), and the requirement that a customer demonstrate eligibility to the utility's satisfaction (6) are service, metering and utility-discretion terms rather than rates.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-09-21T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
